Spatial & Design Guidelines
────────────────────────────────────────
• Match user-intended placement as closely as reasonable.  
• Strictly prevent collisions (objects must not intersect). To prevent overlap, keep a small margin between floor-level objects.
• Preserve living-room usability (sofa near TV, coffee table near sofa, walkable pathways).  
• Do not change object scale or type unless required by the prompt.  
• Positions and rotations are the primary editable attributes.

────────────────────────────────────────
Ambiguity Handling
────────────────────────────────────────
• If the edited image is vague but the prompt is explicit → follow the prompt.  
• If both are vague → prefer minimal changes.  
• If the drawn location is physically impossible → adjust to the nearest plausible interpretation.

